WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.640
At Kew's Millennium Seed Bank,
seeds are dried, then frozen.

2
00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:08.160
It holds seeds of over 40,000 species.

3
00:00:08.210 --> 00:00:13.510
Zoos breed rare animals in captivity,
using studbooks to pair unrelated animals

4
00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:15.230
and limit inbreeding.

5
00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:19.020
So if the last of a species
survives safely in a zoo,

6
00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:21.630
has that species really been saved?

7
00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:26.170
In this mission, you'll weigh the
reasons to conserve biodiversity at all:

8
00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:30.160
ecological, genetic,
economic and aesthetic.

9
00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.690
Then you'll compare
the two big approaches:

10
00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:35.330
protecting a species
in its natural habitat,

11
00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:37.390
and conserving it outside.

12
00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:41.720
Your mission: decide when a
species can really count as saved.
